string.value:
This device did not hand the Java runtime executable memory, so the game runs interpreted instead of just-in-time compiled.

⚠️ This is NOT a defect of the port. It is a restriction of the system:
· HarmonyOS puts anonymous executable memory behind a permission that has to be applied for,
  and that permission is for tablets and PC/2in1 only -- not for phones;
· on a tablet, it means that permission has not taken effect on this device yet.

What it means: the game will be noticeably slower, more so the more units are on screen.
· Measured: load time goes from about 5-6 s to around 20 s;
· a smaller game window helps a lot -- the cost scales with how much you can see;
· full screen with many units will feel slow.
